E1: for m = 0..14 (one random family each; the count does not depend on the exponents): 3-bad at 1 equals '3 divides the sum of the signs' for every signing, and 3 * count + (0 if m even else 2) == 2^m + (2 if m even else 0).  (m, count): [(0, 1), (1, 0), (2, 2), (3, 2), (4, 6), (5, 10), (6, 22), (7, 42), (8, 86), (9, 170), (10, 342), (11, 682), (12, 1366), (13, 2730), (14, 5462)]
    and by the recursion on the three residues of the sum, for every m <= 200
